  "comments": "The ñandu (Rhea Americana) is the biggest bird of South America, similar but smaller to australian ostrich. From 1978 is prohibited to hunt this species, and there is a very successful reproduction program to increase number of animals, and also to production of meat (very low on fat and cholesterol), feathers, and even crystralline lens and cornea for medical uses.<br /><br />\r\nThis coin is part of the series dedicated to native fauna.<br /><br />\r\n<img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5503731014e69.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"380\" height=\"441\" /><br />\r\nÑandú (Rhea americana) - Photografy by Hermann Muñoz<br />\r\nReserva del Cerro Pan de Azúcar, Maldonado (2004)<br /><br />\r\n2011 issue was minted in Royal Mint<br />\r\n2014 issue was minted in Spain<br />\r\n2019 issue was minted in Kremnica",
